{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And all your servants shall come down.</b> He paid honor to the crown — for in the end Pharaoh himself came down to him at night, ״וַיֹּאמֶר קוּמוּ צְּאוּ מִתּוֹךְ עַמִּי״ (Exodus 12), and Moses did not say to him at the start, 'And you shall come down to me and bow to me.'" "<b>Who are at your feet.</b> Those who follow your counsel and your walking." "<b>And after that I shall go out.</b> With all the people from your land." "<b>And he went out from Pharaoh.</b> When he finished his words, he went out from before him." "<b>In hot anger.</b> Because he said to him, ״אַל תֹּסֶף רְאוֹת פָּנַי״ (Exodus 10)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:29.535886495Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}